{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nComplete bridge portability across local shells, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, GitLab CI, and bare\nenvironments without breaking checked-out workflows or environments that still use the legacy\nreconcile vocabulary.\n\nThis story coordinates two independently releasable children:\n\n1. A runner-neutral bridge entrypoint plus thin GitHub Actions, Jenkins, and GitLab wrappers.\n2. Provider-neutral destructive-repair pause ownership for `fsck --repair` and `doctor --repair`.\n\nThe children are intentionally dependency-free and have non-overlapping file impacts. Each must\npreserve old vocabulary, signatures, defaults, messages, exit behavior, and mutation boundaries\nwhile adding the new noun-based bridge route. They may be reviewed and submitted separately or\nshipped together after both gates are green.\n\nGitHub-specific mirror health (`src/rebar/mirror_guard.py`) and optional GitHub step-summary\nreporting are outside bridge execution. They remain unchanged and are not evidence for or against\nthe provider neutrality of the bridge runner.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Review and claim each child independently.\n2. Implement each child under RED-first held-out TDD.\n3. Require `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and no unresolved Gerrit comments before submission.\n4. Verify legacy reconcile callers and checked-out workflows continue to operate.\n5. Close this story after both children have landed and closed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The runner-neutral bridge child is closed with its Gerrit change merged.\n- [x] The provider-neutral destructive-repair child is closed with its Gerrit change merged.\n- [x] Checked-out workflows that still invoke `rebar reconcile --mode ...` retain their behavior.\n- [x] Environments using legacy reconcile modes retain their published defaults and exit behavior.\n- [x] Local, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, GitLab CI, and bare bridge execution use the packaged Python core in `src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py` through exactly `rebar bridge run`; no repository-local runner script is required.\n- [x] Destructive repair no longer depends on the GitHub CLI for schedule safety: `src/rebar/_commands/_repair_pause.py` owns `refs/reconciler/gate`, and `tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py` rejects any `gh` subprocess.\n\n## File impact\n\nOwned by the two child tasks. This coordination story changes no files directly; its recorded file-impact paths are child-owned completion evidence supplied to the bounded close-gate prefetch."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786429009901395001,"uuid":"4a4587d1-970e-4f26-8a17-579a8c05ffb6"}